{
  "schema": "vector.agent-manifest.v2",
  "name": "<BID_DESK_NAME>",
  "capability_id": "supplychain.rfq.quote.v1",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "For a supplier: takes a request for quotation from a buyer's agent, checks who sent it, prices it from the supplier's published price list and returns a quote. The signed receipt of the job is the signed quote.",
  "operator": {
    "name": "Apex Fusion Foundation",
    "contact": "<OPERATOR_CONTACT>"
  },
  "identity": {
    "did": "<AGENT_DID>",
    "registry_address": "",
    "supplier_key": "<AGENT_DID>#<SUPPLIER_PKH>"
  },
  "keys": {
    "supplier_pkh": "<SUPPLIER_PKH>",
    "pub_key_hex": "<SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX>",
    "service_pkh": "<BID_DESK_SERVICE_PKH>"
  },
  "interface": {
    "request_schema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "schema",
        "sender_did",
        "delegation",
        "rfq"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "schema": {
          "const": "vector.usecase.rfq.v1"
        },
        "sender_did": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^did:vector:[0-9a-f]{64}$",
          "description": "The DID of the buyer's agent that sends the request"
        },
        "delegation": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
          "description": "The identifier of the delegation that names the sender as its delegate and paid for the job"
        },
        "rfq": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "rfq_id",
            "items",
            "needed_by"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "rfq_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$",
              "description": "The identifier of the request: 1 to 64 characters, letters, digits, dots, hyphens and underscores, starting with a letter or a digit"
            },
            "items": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 1,
              "maxItems": 20,
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "sku",
                  "quantity"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "properties": {
                  "sku": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$",
                    "description": "The SKU: 1 to 64 characters, letters, digits, dots, hyphens and underscores, starting with a letter or a digit"
                  },
                  "quantity": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 1000000,
                    "description": "The quantity that the buyer wants: a whole number from 1 to 1000000"
                  }
                }
              },
              "description": "The items to quote: 1 to 20, and each SKU once"
            },
            "needed_by": {
              "type": "string",
              "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$",
              "description": "The date by which the goods are needed, as YYYY-MM-DD, a date that exists"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "response_schema": {
      "$ref": "https://github.com/Apex-Fusion/vector-service-agents/blob/main/specs/bid-desk.md#response"
    },
    "routes": {
      "job": "/v1/job",
      "status": "/status",
      "capability": "/capability",
      "price_list": "/price-list.json"
    },
    "notes": [
      "The request is the message of use case 3 (supplier bid evaluation): its schema is vector.usecase.rfq.v1, and it holds the DID of the sender, the delegation and a request for quotation of 1 to 20 items. A request that breaks a rule of the intake is refused with bad_shape (400).",
      "Before the runtime claims the escrow, the service checks the sender, the delegation, the payment from a vault, and that it quoted no request with this identifier for this sender. A check that fails is a refusal with its code (403), and the escrow stays open. A source that cannot be read is 503 check_unavailable. The service takes no approval.",
      "After the Claim, one model call prices the request from the price list. The service checks that each line is an item of the request, and it makes the line totals, the total and the longest lead time.",
      "The price list is served at /price-list.json, and its SHA-256 is in behaviour.price_list. Each Bid Desk has its own price list, so each has its own manifest hash.",
      "The quote names the hash of the request and the hash of the price list, and it holds the credential of the desk. The signed receipt of the job is the signed quote."
    ]
  },
  "terms": {
    "price_lovelace": 1000000,
    "supplier_bond_lovelace": 1000000,
    "buyer_bond_lovelace": 1000000,
    "max_processing_ms": 480000,
    "input_limits": {
      "request_bytes": 900000
    }
  },
  "behaviour": {
    "data_handling": "The request for quotation and the price list are synthetic data, and they are held in memory while a job runs. The service writes to its state directory the bookkeeping of the escrows that it posts for its model call and the book of the requests that it answered (the sender, the request identifier and the hash of the quote of each). The log carries job outcomes, counts and codes, never a request, a quote, a credential or a key.",
    "third_parties": [
      "the identity gateway (the resolution of the DID of the sender, and the request for the credential of this agent)",
      "the ledger, read only (the delegation and the escrow paid from a vault)",
      "a model supplier on the Vector marketplace, hired through a bonded escrow, and the model provider behind it (the prompt of the decision: the request for quotation and the price list)"
    ],
    "claim": {
      "statements": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "text": "The unit price of every line in a quote is the price its published price list gives for that SKU and quantity."
        },
        {
          "id": "S2",
          "text": "A quote names the hash of the request for quotation it answers."
        },
        {
          "id": "S3",
          "text": "This agent gives one quote per request for quotation and sender."
        }
      ]
    },
    "fault_modes": [
      "quote_off_price_list"
    ],
    "model": {
      "allowlist": [
        "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"
      ],
      "max_price_lovelace": 1000000
    },
    "relying_on": {
      "mock_systems": [],
      "gateway_routes": [
        "GET /1.0/identifiers/{did}",
        "GET /agents/{id}/credential"
      ]
    },
    "price_list": {
      "uri": "<PRICE_LIST_URI>",
      "sha256": "<PRICE_LIST_SHA256>"
    }
  },
  "status": {
    "chip": "proposed",
    "since": "2026-11-24"
  },
  "gaps": [
    "A quote is the result of a paid job. It is not a binding offer.",
    "The model prices the request. Nothing in this agent checks its lines against the price list: the buyer's agent can, because the price list and its hash are public.",
    "The three Bid Desks are one code base under three records, run by one foundation. They do not compete.",
    "The compliance attestation is issued by a demonstration registry with no record of its own.",
    "The numbers of the price list are synthetic.",
    "The controller key of this deployment, the Accountable key and the guardian keys are on one host of one operator, so a party is independent of the controller by key only.",
    "What this does not show: no run covers the refund of the escrow of a revoked agent, the reclaim of an escrow in use case 3, or a relying party that refuses a live token after its authority ends. Tests cover that last case only.",
    "This service has a fault switch for failure runs with these possible values: quote_off_price_list (one quote line has a unit price that is not the published price for that item and quantity); this manifest is the same for every value, so only the field fault_mode of each result shows which value is active."
  ],
  "links": {
    "spec": "https://github.com/Apex-Fusion/vector-service-agents/blob/main/specs/bid-desk.md",
    "source": "https://github.com/Apex-Fusion/vector-service-agents/tree/main/agents/bid-desk",
    "explorer_advert": ""
  }
}
